A couple of things:

Autopickup exceptions also include whatever name you give the item. So
if you only want to pick up daggers that you fired, add an autopickup
for "<* named Q" and then name the stuff in your quiver "Q". You can
use the single exception for daggers, arrows, darts and whatever.

Another semiuseful one I learned from sourcediving (sorry) was to chat
with your housepet to find out if they need food. It's useful for
knights and if you're trying to rob a store by waiting.
Cats yowl when in trouble or going untame, meow when hungry, mew when
going hungry and purr when ok.
Dogs (when not a full moon night) whine when in trouble, going untame
or hungry, bark when getting hungry and yip when ok.
Horses neigh when going untame, whinnies if hungry and whicker when
ok.

Unfortuantely horses don't warn you before they get hungry, only
aftwerwards.

